{{!< default}}
{{!-- WHS Brief: public Change Tracker (/tracker/).

Not to be confused with /register/ (register.hbs), which is paid-member-only
and shows full item content grouped by jurisdiction. This page is the
opposite on purpose: public, headline + date only, no analysis — the doc
this was built from calls it "the best SEO asset available in this market
because it answers the exact query people type."

How this works:
  - Each week, whs-legislative-brief-weekly creates/updates one small ALWAYS-
    PUBLIC post tagged #tracker (visibility: public, never paid) containing
    just compact .wbd-tracker-item entries (headline link + date + status,
    no description). This page fetches the last ~52 of those posts (roughly
    12 months at one per week) into a hidden container, and tracker.js (see
    assets/js/tracker.js) walks it, flattens every .wbd-tracker-item across
    all of them into one list, sorts newest first, and caps display to the
    last 12 months.
  - No member-gating fallback branch is needed here (unlike register.hbs) —
    #tracker posts are never gated, so {{content}} always renders in full for
    every visitor.
  - The jurisdiction filter row below links to the 9 real /jurisdiction/{slug}/
    pages (crawlable, not JS-only) for SEO, plus a couple of JS-only filters
    (National, Standards) that don't have their own dedicated URL since the
    automation brief only asked for one page per state/territory and NZ.
--}}

<main id="site-main" class="site-main outer">
<div class="inner posts">

    <div class="whs-brief-doc">
        <div class="wbd-masthead">
            <p class="wbd-eyebrow">Work Health &amp; Safety — Change Tracker</p>
            <h1>Every WHS/OHS legislative change, tracked</h1>
            <p class="wbd-dek">Every Act, Regulation, Code of practice and Standard change we've covered in the last 12 months across Australia and New Zealand. Headline and date only — for the full story on any item, including what it means and what to do about it, see the weekly brief.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <nav class="wbd-tracker-filters" aria-label="Filter by jurisdiction">
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/tracker/" class="wbd-tracker-filter is-active" data-jur="all">All</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/tracker/" class="wbd-tracker-filter" data-jur="national">National</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/nsw/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">NSW</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/vic/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">VIC</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/qld/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">QLD</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/wa/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">WA</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/sa/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">SA</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/tas/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">TAS</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/act/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">ACT</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/nt/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">NT</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/jurisdiction/nz/" class="wbd-tracker-filter">NZ</a>
        <a href="{{@site.url}}/tracker/" class="wbd-tracker-filter" data-jur="standards">Standards</a>
    </nav>

    <div id="wbd-tracker-output" class="wbd-tracker-output">
        <p class="wbd-tracker-loading">Loading tracker…</p>
    </div>

    <p class="wbd-register-footnote">Showing changes from roughly the last 12 months. Want the analysis, not just the headline? <a href="{{@site.url}}/brief/">Subscribe to the full weekly brief</a>.</p>

    {{!-- Hidden source data: full content of recent #tracker posts, for
    tracker.js to parse. Never shown directly. --}}
    <div id="wbd-tracker-source" hidden>
        {{#get "posts" filter="tag:tracker" limit="52" order="published_at desc" as |posts|}}
            {{#foreach posts}}
                {{content}}
            {{/foreach}}
        {{/get}}
    </div>

</div>
</main>
